     EXPLANATION OF OPTION
 
     Use this option to determine what help is available in the 
     drive window and how to quit in ace.
 
     NOTE:  A procedure to access help about the options in the 
            drive window is included in the help screens following 
            the explanation of this option.
 
     ABOUT THE HELP
 
     Help information is provided for each option in the drive window.  
     This help may include the following information:
 
          - An explanation of the option
          - Examples
          - Procedures
          - References for more information
 
     Remember, see the User Guide for more information about the 
     option.
                                (CONTINUED)
     PROCEDURE -- ACCESSING HELP IN THE LOGICAL UNIT WINDOW
 
     1.   Press "h" to access help for the options in the logical unit
          window.
 
     2.   Press a key corresponding to one of the options in the
          help menu.  For example, press "c" for information
          about creating a logical unit.
 
 
     ABOUT UPDATING/REFRESHING ACE
 
     To update/refresh the Array Configuration Editor, press <U> at 
     any time.
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
                                (CONTINUED)
     ABOUT QUITTING IN ACE
 
     To quit operations while using the Array Configuration Editor, 
     press the "q" key.  You may quit the following:
 
          - "Popboxes" (messages displayed in boxes)
          - An operation in either the drive or drive window
          - The "Help" menu
          - A "Help" option
 
     Note that once you actually initiate an operation, you can NOT 
     quit the operation by pressing the "q" key.  For example, once 
     you press "d" to delete a drive, the array controller deletes the 
     drive you specified.  
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
                                (CONTINUED)
     Also note that the Array Configuration Editor may display a 
     popbox with the option to continue or quit an operation before it 
     actually initiates the operation.  This gives you an opportunity 
     to reconsider, before initiating the operation.  For example, 
     after you press "f" to fail a drive, the following popbox is 
     displayed:
 
          +============= < Information > ==========+
          |                                        |
          | If you fail a drive, you may lose data |
          | redundancy.                            |
          |                                        |
          | Press 'c' to continue,                 |
          | or press 'q' to quit.                  |
          +========================================+
